                <pb facs="0405" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3104</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chairman of the Commission of
                        Neutrals</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-05-08">May 8, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Neutral Commission met and I gave the members copies of the circular telegram
                    of the Bolivian Government to its Legations abroad which had been left with me
                    by Mr. Finot on Saturday. I also told them of the conversation I had had on
                    Saturday with the Paraguayan Minister. As a result, it was decided to ask the
                    neighboring countries to meet with us on the following day, Tuesday, May
                    ninth.</p>
                <closer><signed>F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">rancis</hi>] W[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">hite</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
